  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "Bus executive Francis Tedesco has represented motorcoach operators in discussions about safety oversight and drivers’ working hours. At Academy, the training programme described during his early presidency required recruits to spend at least forty hours behind the wheel, regardless of previous experience. Driver records, further instruction and incentive programmes formed part of the operating system.\n\nThe company also recognises drivers through awards named for its founder, Frank Tedesco. These acknowledge safety, customer service and length of employment. After pandemic disruption, Academy announced the return of local award ceremonies, giving drivers public recognition within the markets where they worked.",
    "html": "<p>Bus executive Francis Tedesco has represented motorcoach operators in discussions about safety oversight and drivers’ working hours. At Academy, the training programme described during his early presidency required recruits to spend at least forty hours behind the wheel, regardless of previous experience. Driver records, further instruction and incentive programmes formed part of the operating system.</p>\r\n<p>The company also recognises drivers through awards named for its founder, Frank Tedesco. These acknowledge safety, customer service and length of employment. After pandemic disruption, Academy announced the return of local award ceremonies, giving drivers public recognition within the markets where they worked.</p>\r\n",
